.TH FL-CHARMAP 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-charmap \- character map
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-charmap\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browses the Unicode characters by block, in any installed font. The details
pane shows the character's name, code point, UTF-8 bytes and HTML entity.
Search by name ("right arrow"), by the character itself or by hex code
("U+2192", "2192"). Double-click a character to add it to the text field and
press \fBCopy\fR to put the text on the clipboard. "Only in this font"
hides code points the font (via fontconfig) does not cover.
.PP
Character names come from \fIUnicodeData.txt\fR (Debian package
\fBunicode-data\fR, Arch package \fBunicode-character-database\fR); without
it, search works on code points and block names only.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/share/fldesktop/charmap/Blocks.txt\fR
Unicode block list.
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/charmap.ini\fR
Font, size and recently used characters.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-edit\fR(1)
